# Trivy suppressions. One rule, one reason, one line each.
#
# Phase: 1 - Contracts & First Agent Path
#
# This file rather than an inline `# trivy:ignore:` comment because trivy scans
# the RENDERED Helm output, and rendering strips template comments - an inline
# suppression in a chart template silently does nothing. That is the same shape
# as the pnpm overrides that sat in package.json where pnpm no longer reads
# them: a fix that looks applied and changes nothing.
#
# Threshold stays CRITICAL,HIGH. Suppressing one rule with a reason is not the
# same as lowering the bar, and nothing here may be added without one.

# KSV-0109 "ConfigMap with secrets" fires on LLM_MAX_TOKENS because the key
# contains "TOKEN". It is a token COUNT - an integer request limit - and every
# real credential in this chart comes from a Secret, never from the ConfigMap
# (see minio-secret.yaml and the secretRef entries in api-deployment.yaml).
#
# The identical name-shape trap caught this repository's own secret guard,
# which flagged LLM_MAX_TOKENS and S3_ACCESS_KEY before being rewritten to
# derive credential-ness from the settings model rather than from the name.
KSV-0109
